  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader with a long topic title, and above all with VoiceOver or a large text size, I want the full title shown by the title pill to stay until I dismiss it and to be fully readable on an iPhone, so that the only way to read a truncated title does not disappear while I read it.\n\n### Rule\n\n- \"Minimize use of time-boxed interface elements. Views and controls that auto-dismiss on a timer can be problematic for people who need longer to process information, and for people who use assistive technologies that require more time to traverse the interface. Prefer dismissing views with an explicit action.\" — [HIG › Accessibility](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/accessibility) (Cognitive; page updated 2025-06-09).\n- \"Avoid displaying popovers in compact views. […] Reserve popovers for wide views; for compact views, use all available screen space by presenting information in a full-screen modal view like a sheet instead.\" — [HIG › Popovers](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/popovers) (iOS, iPadOS).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/ScreenTitle/ScreenTitle.swift`:\n- `:48` `static let foldDelay = Duration.seconds(4)` and `:178-182` `.task(id: state.isExpanded) { … try? await Task.sleep(for: TitlePillState.foldDelay); state.fold() }`: the popover closes after 4 s, whatever the title length, also under VoiceOver or Switch Control.\n- `:160` `.lineLimit(1)`: the pill truncates, so the popover is the only way to read a long title.\n- `:169-174` `.popover(isPresented: $state.isExpanded) { Text(title)….presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover) }`: the popover is forced in compact width; its content is a plain `Text` with no `ScrollView`.\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nNo counterpart: legacy uses the system navigation title (`HFRswift/Swift/MainWindow.swift:195`, `:802`). The pill is SwiftHFR's (#977, #978).\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect** for the timer (accessibility, SwiftHFR-only). The forced popover is the operator's design of #978: (b) unless the Mac check shows clipping at large text sizes.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- Remove the fold timer: the popover's own dismissal (tap outside, second tap on the pill) already closes it.\n- Drop `.presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)` so compact width gets the system adaptation (a sheet with a small detent), or keep the popover and wrap the title in a `ScrollView`.\n- Check: a unit test on `TitlePillState` (nothing folds without a tap). Mac check: iPhone portrait, a long title at AX5 and under VoiceOver: the whole title is readable and stays until dismissed.\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
